# m9_ct_capacity_shrink: exactly-sized blocks for the packed input and its residual copy after the mod
# switch (instead of the capacity of their creation level).
# Position 9 on m8_chunked_bootstrap; rule 4 against m8's peak table (121.6 GiB, 127,528,816 kB; zen4,
# 16-core cpuset, shared node, pmsample_chain; run m9r_ct_capacity_shrink).
#
# impl_lever: patch_ct_capacity_shrink.py
# impl_base_image: image:moai-cpu-m8_chunked_bootstrap.sif
#
# pool_attacked: host
# object_attacked: all_layer_test()  <- seal::Ciphertext::operator=
# object_skipped: batch_input(std::vector
# cost_class: free
# evidence: equivalent
# plaintext_equivalence: impl/equiv_layer_outputs.py
# not_selectable_until: m8_chunked_bootstrap
# phase_effect: after_attention
#
# ---------------------------------------------------------------------------------------------
# table      m8's peak (121.6 GiB, Layer-0 attention; by allocation site):
#              28.2 GB  22.1%  all_layer_test() (test_full_scheme.hpp:989)  <- seal::Ciphertext::operator=   (enc_ecd_x_copy: 768 ciphertexts mod-switched in place from 35 to 21 limbs, still holding the 35-limb capacity)
#              28.2 GB  22.1%  batch_input (Batch_encode_encrypt.hpp:32)  <- seal::Encryptor::encrypt_internal   (enc_ecd_x, the encrypted input, same capacity slack; live, read by every head)
#              17.2 GB  13.5%  all_layer_test() (test_full_scheme.hpp:918)  <- keygenerator.h:208:create_galois_keys   (attention keys, live)
#              14.5 GB  11.4%  stage_softmax_load_boot_phase (softmax.hpp:29)  <- kswitchkeys.h:239   (softmax bootstrap keys, live)
#              13.3 GB  10.4%  ct_ct_matrix_mul_colpacking   (QK^T temporaries)
#              12.1 GB   9.5%  single_att_block (single_att_block.hpp:73)   (enc_X_v, capacity slack; m15's object)
#               6.7 GB   5.3%  sealpool:retained
# choice     SEAL keeps DynArray capacity on in-place mod switch: copy (:989) and input hold 35-limb blocks
#            for 21-limb content (28.2 GB each for 16.9 GB of data). Copy into a fresh Ciphertext and move
#            back (copy-assign allocates by size); applied to both (input skipped as a release target, same
#            helper shrinks it). Same bytes, free. Enabler: m8's chunking exposed the attention block.
# measured   attention 121.6 -> 95.6 GiB; global peak moves to the FFN window (after_final; 120.3 in m8,
#            122.8 here), inside the 2.0 pp spread (off-path.md): plateau step (rule 5).
# gate       bit-identical to m7 (md5 dc043a0b); equivalent to m0 through m6.
# RESULT (measured): peak 127,528,816 -> 128,774,692 kB (121.6 -> 122.8 GiB, +0.98%), wall 125,371 s, gate md5 dc043a0b. Phase: Layer-0 attention 121.6 -> 95.6 GiB (per-marker sample); new global peak: Layer-0 FFN window (after_final, marker 13).
# REFUTED IF the LEVER|ct_capacity_shrink markers are absent from markers.txt, or the attention phase did not fall by more than the spread. A global-peak move inside the spread is expected here (plateau) and is not a refutation of the lever.
